        "body": "FreeBindCraft runs faster on Apple Silicon, with performance optimizations enabled by default.\n\n- Improved MetalJAX loop compilation, attention kernels, and weight conversion.\n- Unchunked execution by default for speed, with optional chunking for lower memory use on larger jobs.\n- A shorter installation and usage guide.\n- New M5 Max benchmarks against six NVIDIA GPU systems, covering both PyRosetta and OpenMM/FASPR workflows.\n\nThe M5 Max completed the small benchmark in about four minutes and the larger CA2 benchmark in about 33 minutes. Timings include compilation and downstream processing; the benchmark page describes the workloads and results.\n\n[Apple Silicon guide](https://github.com/cytokineking/FreeBindCraft/blob/v1.0.7/apple_silicon/README.md) · [Benchmark figures](https://github.com/cytokineking/FreeBindCraft/blob/v1.0.7/apple_silicon/benchmarks/README.md)\n\nTo update an existing Apple Silicon installation, pull the latest code and rerun `bash install_bindcraft.sh`.\n",
